# Handoff: Ryanair Agent Simulator - UI restyle shipped (theme system live)

## What just shipped
- Full UI restyle onto a semantic CSS-variable palette, with a dark default and a light theme toggle.
- `tailwind.config.js`: `darkMode: ''class''` plus semantic colours (canvas, surface, surface-2, surface-3, line, line-strong, ink, ink-2, ink-3, ink-4, on-brand, brand, brand-strong, accent, accent-ink, ok, ok-strong, warn, warn-strong, danger, danger-strong) defined as `rgb(var(--c-*) / <alpha-value>)` so opacity modifiers still work.
- `src/index.css`: `:root` = light tokens, `.dark` = dark tokens, `color-scheme` per theme, themed scrollbars, subtle theme transition.
- `src/theme.js`: `loadTheme` / `saveTheme` / `applyTheme` / `nextTheme`, key `ryanair-agent-simulator.theme`, dark default, defensive reads (same pattern as settings.js/history.js).
- `index.html`: inline pre-paint script applies the saved theme so there is no wrong-palette flash.
- `App.jsx`: theme state + effect (apply + persist), Sun/Moon toggle in the header; header restyled to a surface bar with a brand logo mark and a gold accent hairline; setup hero with capability chips; case cards `rounded-2xl` with hover lift and a selected ring/check; KpiTile + dashboard panel + empty states restyled; chat message meta contrast fixed; conflicting macro-button classes cleaned up; `selectedScenario` reads in the setup screen are now optional-chained.
- All ~140 raw colour utilities were migrated by a one-shot codemod (459 rewrites, 0 unmapped, 0 leftovers); the codemod was deleted after use.
- Responsiveness pass: root uses `h-dvh`; header wraps (brand row + KPI HUD strip that scrolls horizontally on narrow screens); the 3-panel workspace collapses to a Case/Chat/Policy pane switcher below `lg` (columns are `lg:col-span-*` only, so the mobile 1-column grid cannot be squeezed); setup and scorecard screens scroll safely instead of clipping (`my-auto` pattern instead of `justify-center` + overflow); modals are capped at `max-h-[92dvh]` with internal scroll and single-column forms on phones; cards/scorecard grids step down at `sm`/`md`/`lg`/`xl`; buttons go full-width on phones.
- Verified after the responsiveness pass: build OK, `MISSING: 0` (315 utilities), SSR smoke 12/12, and an audit confirming zero unprefixed `col-span-*` / `grid-cols-{3+}` remain.

## Verification performed
- `npm run build` passes.
- `node scripts/check-tw-coverage.mjs` -> `MISSING: 0` (287 utilities).
- SSR smoke render of the setup screen: 12/12 PASS (toggle present, no raw palette classes in the rendered HTML).
- `theme.js` logic: 15/15 PASS (defaults, validation, hostile storage, applyTheme class + colorScheme).
- Built CSS contains both `:root` and `.dark` token blocks and 85 `rgb(var(--c-*))` references; `dist/index.html` carries the pre-paint script.

## Known gaps / next steps
- The light theme and the responsive breakpoints were verified structurally, not visually: toggle the theme and resize the window through ~360 / 768 / 1024 / 1440px, checking the setup screen, chat panes, both modals and the scorecard.
- Temp verifiers were deleted; consider permanent tests for `theme.js` and the palette mapping.
- `App.jsx` is still a ~1950-line monolith: extracting SetupScreen / ChatView / KpiSidebar / Scorecard / Modals is the natural next refactor, behaviour-identical.
- Stray legacy files still tracked: `airline/scripts/extract-llm.mjs`, `airline/tests/llm.test.js`.

## Build / verify loop
1. `cd airline; npm run build`
2. `node scripts/check-tw-coverage.mjs` -> `MISSING: 0` (ALWAYS run after the build; it reads `dist/`).
3. `npm run preview` (:4173) to click-test; `/llm-proxy/v1` exists in dev/preview only, never on Pages.
4. `git push` -> `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` builds with `VITE_PUBLIC_BASE=/cura/` -> https://spanexx.github.io/cura/

## Gotchas
- The remote intentionally holds ONLY `airline/`, `.github/workflows/` and `sessions/`.
- Editor tool: keep each edit under ~6000 chars; never parallel-edit the same file with the same anchor.
- `App.jsx` line numbers shift after every edit - re-read the region before anchoring the next edit.
- PowerShell here-strings mangle GitHub expression syntax; prefer the editor tool for file writes.
- GitHub API calls from PowerShell need a User-Agent header or they 403.
